steps=2 ANSWER: "**Most consistent driver in the 2024 season**\n\nUsing the standard deviation of finishing positions across all 24 races as a measure of consistency, the driver with the lowest spread was **Valtteri Bottas**.\n\n| Driver | Full name | Races entered | Avg. finishing position | Position SD |\n|--------|-----------|---------------|--------------------------|-------------|\n| BOT | Valtteri Bottas | 24 | 15.83 | **2.22** |\n\n*Bottas’s standard deviation of 2.22 is the smallest among all drivers who raced in every round, indicating the tightest spread of results.*  \n\n**Method**  \n- Queried the `results` table for all race (`session = 'R'`) rows.  \n- Joined to `driver_seasons` to get the full driver name.  \n- Calculated `STDDEV_SAMP(Position)` for each driver and sorted ascending.  \n- Included only drivers who participated in all 24 races (the query naturally filtered out those with fewer entries).  \n\nThus, Valtteri Bottas was the most consistent driver in the 2024 Formula 1 races."
